  "removed_guidance": {
    "0": [
      {
        "rect": [
          23.8,
          700.7959716796875,
          585.834765625,
          714.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "The cover sheet of the exam should tell the students how many of each sheet in the test they should have (how "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          23.8,
          714.7959716796875,
          590.0311767578125,
          728.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "many answer sheets, image sheets, etc.). Students should be encouraged to check that they have all test pages "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          23.8,
          728.7959716796875,
          573.7206909179688,
          742.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "before beginning the test. Students should also be made aware of any differences in point value for different "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          23.8,
          742.7959716796875,
          590.189501953125,
          756.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "questions or sections of the test in case they wish to allocate their time proportionately. If students must submit "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          23.8,
          756.7959716796875,
          486.33803100585936,
          770.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "an answer sheet to be graded, they should be made aware of this before beginning the test."
      }
    ],
    "4": [
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          606.7959716796875,
          558.211962890625,
          620.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "It is best to label image sheets if there are more than one, so that students save time looking for images "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          620.7959716796875,
          544.7347900390625,
          634.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "referenced in the questions. This can aid in sorting the images by question type i.e. images of surface "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          634.7959716796875,
          569.0228759765625,
          648.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "features on one page and images of missions and spectral features on another page. Tests should be long "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          648.7959716796875,
          582.6176025390625,
          662.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "because they have many or more difficult questions, not because test formatting makes answering questions "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          662.7959716796875,
          76.448046875,
          676.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "tedious.  "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          676.7959716796875,
          33.2,
          690.80400390625
        ],
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          65.8,
          676.7959716796875,
          567.053515625,
          690.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "When creating image sheets for a test, it is usually easier to prepare sets of images, along with any "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          690.7959716796875,
          569.2136108398438,
          704.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "labels or lettering/numbering, in a separate document and then screenshot or export the set of images for "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          704.7959716796875,
          568.5958129882813,
          718.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "use in your test, to avoid formatting problems. Keep in mind when preparing image sheets that the images "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          718.7959716796875,
          583.5429565429688,
          732.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "most easily accessible to you (usually from the internet) are also those most accessible to students preparing "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          732.7959716796875,
          571.9423706054688,
          746.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "for the event. The object of image identification is to test both understanding and preparation; Test authors "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          746.7959716796875,
          560.9852783203125,
          760.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "are discouraged from including too many obscure images that only reward rote memorization rather than "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          29.8,
          760.7959716796875,
          130.88119812011718,
          774.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "holistic preparation."
      }
    ],
    "5": [],
    "6": [],
    "7": [],
    "8": [
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          189.79600219726564,
          536.9144165039063,
          203.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "Section A of this test is an example of common style of B Division astronomy event exams. Some "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          203.79600219726564,
          559.847705078125,
          217.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "questions are very easy, and some are very difficult - either because they require critical thinking and "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          217.79600219726564,
          550.7491943359375,
          231.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "understanding about the concepts in the rules, or because they require more complete preparation "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          231.79600219726564,
          527.2723876953125,
          245.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "and knowledge of the objects. Many of the questions require image recognition and secondary "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          245.79600219726564,
          374.9708740234375,
          259.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "questions build off correct identification of an image, but not all. "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          273.79600219726564,
          553.8560668945313,
          287.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "Relevant information about past, current, and future missions is often the most challenging for both "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          287.79600219726564,
          560.747607421875,
          301.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "students and proctors to distinguish from irrelevant information, as there is no clear line that dictates "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          301.79600219726564,
          542.81474609375,
          315.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "which missions or which instruments comprising those missions are directly relevant to studies of "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          315.79600219726564,
          538.1324951171875,
          329.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "geology in the solar system as outlined in the rules. Be careful with questions about timelines for "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          329.79600219726564,
          554.60966796875,
          343.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "progress of future missions because timescales for these missions tend to change frequently. When "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          47.8,
          343.79600219726564,
          560.19560546875,
          357.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "used on a test, answers should reflect the most recent official statement made on the date of launch."
      }
    ],
    "9": [
      {
        "rect": [
          38.8,
          603.7959716796875,
          552.3129760742188,
          617.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "Section B of this exam differs from Section A primarily in that it tests concepts related more closely to "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          38.8,
          617.7959716796875,
          557.9564697265625,
          631.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "Part II of the event rules than Part I. It is not necessary to separate the concepts in these two sections, "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          38.8,
          631.7959716796875,
          538.9063598632813,
          645.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "as some concepts lend themselves more readily to applications to the objects outlined in Part I (as "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          38.8,
          645.7959716796875,
          309.99315185546874,
          659.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "seen in Section A and in the next section, Section C.   "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          38.8,
          673.7959716796875,
          549.7194091796875,
          687.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "It is not necessary to split the test into “Sections” but it is a good idea to employ some organizational "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          38.8,
          687.7959716796875,
          469.7396728515625,
          701.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "structure spanning the pages of the test in case students elect to split the test apart. "
      }
    ],
    "10": [],
    "11": [
      {
        "rect": [
          75.8,
          610.7959716796875,
          516.5184814453125,
          624.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "Some questions in Section D, as well as Section C, are math questions that require the "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          75.8,
          624.7959716796875,
          510.6397277832031,
          638.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "use of the calculator. The mathematical components of the concepts being tested are "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          75.8,
          638.7959716796875,
          514.06572265625,
          652.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "reasonable for middle schoolers, and questions using these concepts that use “clean” "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          75.8,
          652.7959716796875,
          423.79323120117186,
          666.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "numbers that do not require the use of a calculator could be written. "
      }
    ],
    "12": [
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          522.7959716796875,
          411.85753173828124,
          536.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "With regards to Answer Sheets and Answer Keys (following pages): "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          536.7959716796875,
          538.9003784179688,
          550.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "It is typically a good idea to include space for team number and name on all answer sheets, "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          550.7959716796875,
          493.8463623046875,
          564.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "in case tests become disorganized, and in case there is some confusion with team "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          564.7959716796875,
          510.8913146972656,
          578.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "numbers. A key should usually be printed and recorded in the same format as the test "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          578.7959716796875,
          530.87724609375,
          592.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "answer sheets to speed the grading process and assist any volunteer graders who may be "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          592.7959716796875,
          524.3226806640625,
          606.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "working with you grading tests. Efficiency is especially important when a large number of "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          606.7959716796875,
          518.807666015625,
          620.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "tests must be graded and ranked in time for the awards ceremony. Note that a different "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          620.7959716796875,
          519.342822265625,
          634.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "amount of space is allotted for different questions to assist students in keeping track of "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          634.7959716796875,
          531.9164306640625,
          648.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "answers. It is important to provide answer spaces large enough for larger handwriting. It is "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          649.0999877929687,
          112.51999969482422,
          663.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "highly "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          112.11999969482422,
          649.7959716796875,
          535.1468994140625,
          663.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "recommended that a test author take his or her own tests several times throughout "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          663.7959716796875,
          526.7023193359375,
          677.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "its development to check for inconsistencies in numbering, oddly phrased questions, and "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          677.7959716796875,
          527.1619140625,
          691.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "inconveniences like answer spaces that are not large enough for adequate answers to be "
      },
      {
        "rect": [
          74.8,
          691.7959716796875,
          187.4300109863281,
          705.80400390625
        ],
        "text": "comfortably provided. "
      }
    ],
